WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.625
Sovereign AI systems need observability because private operation does not remove

00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:06.020
operational uncertainty.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.580
Teams need to understand how systems are used, whether they are performing well,

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:11.600
whether sensitive data is handled correctly,

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:14.110
and whether outputs are reliable enough for the workflow.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:18.120
Useful signals may include request volume, latency, model errors, retrieval quality,

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.600
tool calls, user feedback, safety events, cost signals, and operational failures.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:25.190
Prompt and response logging require careful design.

00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:29.135
Logs are useful for debugging, evaluation, abuse investigation, and support,

00:00:29.135 --> 00:00:33.425
but they may contain confidential business data, personal information, customer material,

00:00:33.425 --> 00:00:34.920
or other sensitive content.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:39.340
A responsible logging plan includes redaction, retention limits, access controls,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.535
sampling, privacy review,

00:00:40.535 --> 00:00:44.805
and a clear distinction between operational telemetry and sensitive content capture.

00:00:44.805 --> 00:00:47.350
Evaluation turns observation into improvement.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.790
Teams may evaluate answer quality, groundedness, retrieval accuracy, refusal behavior,

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:55.660
workflow completion, user satisfaction, and recurring failure patterns.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:59.530
Evaluation should be connected to model version, retrieval collection, prompt template,

00:00:59.530 --> 00:01:03.800
runtime configuration, and deployment environment so teams can understand what changed.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:06.930
The goal is accountable operation, not uncontrolled surveillance.

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:10.620
Monitoring should help teams detect failures, improve quality, manage cost,

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.535
and enforce policy without creating a new privacy problem.

00:01:13.535 --> 00:01:17.645
A sovereign AI program should make logs and evaluation data useful, protected,

00:01:17.645 --> 00:01:20.095
and limited to legitimate operational purposes.

00:01:20.095 --> 00:01:23.660
It also helps to define who is allowed to review sensitive observations.

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:25.765
Engineers may need operational metrics.

00:01:25.765 --> 00:01:28.525
Privacy and security teams may need selected evidence.

00:01:28.525 --> 00:01:30.895
Product owners may need aggregate quality trends.

00:01:30.895 --> 00:01:33.540
These views should not all expose the same raw content.

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.090
Good observability separates signal from exposure,

00:01:36.090 --> 00:01:40.640
giving each role enough information to act without broadening access unnecessarily.
